@startuml
title Node progress display projection - ADR-019 (not persisted enums)
[*] --> PENDING : known plan, not started
[*] --> RETAINED : verified retain/binding evidence
[*] --> UNKNOWN : missing/unsupported observation
PENDING --> WAITING : required provider unfinished
PENDING --> PROVISIONING : persisted attempt/workload start
WAITING --> PROVISIONING : providers ready + observed start
PROVISIONING --> CHECKING : persisted readiness stage
CHECKING --> READY : validated readiness completed
PROVISIONING --> READY : explicit Ready fact, no intermediate observation
PROVISIONING --> FAILED : safe persisted failure
CHECKING --> FAILED : safe persisted failure
WAITING --> BLOCKED : failed provider proven by graph
PENDING --> BLOCKED : failed provider proven by graph
RETAINED --> PROVISIONING : explicit later attempt supersedes intent
UNKNOWN --> PENDING : sufficient consistent observation
UNKNOWN --> READY : explicit matching Ready fact
note right of UNKNOWN
No timer-driven state changes.
Missing row never means Ready.
Poll failure marks view stale; preserves observation.
end note
note bottom of FAILED
No implication of cleanup/rollback.
Preserve completed peers and exact attempt identity.
Existing execution lifecycle remains authoritative.
end note
@enduml
